Ascended my samurai today.  This is the first game I was geno less and
polyless.  The h's, L's, and ;'s weren't as bad as I thought.  I always
had a fire wand so mind flayers didn't worry me, Lichs are easy to take
care of but annoying for their cursing, and the water species weren't
bad even on the plane of water.

The most remarkable part about the early game was how many times I went
back through the dungeon, the mines, and sobokan looking for silver
dragons.  I found them but no scales were dropped.  So I broke wishless
for that SDSM and kept on wishing.  My armor was sorely lacking and my
AC was a paltry -12.  When I was done it was a -30 and I had GoP, HoT,
SDSM, the spell identify, and a +7 Snickersnee.

I killed the priest in VotD for books but forgot to look for a robe so
I wished for one and then later noticed that robe.  Duh!

I disenchanted my +4 armor to +3 but only found one more ?oEA and that
was right before the I got the BotD.  Molochs sanctum was a snap
because I got a c corpse in the graveyard before the temple area and I
subsequently stoned everything that moved.

The run up was definitely the MOST ANNOYING ascension I've ever had.
My knight wasn't nearly this bad.  He was thrown back twice the whole
time.  As for my samurai, lets put it this way:

BOTTOM : D51

ORCUS TOWN: D41

I saw the stairs up to Orcus Town six times.  I thought I would never
get out of there.  And when I was one leve below the VotD I was thrown
back 2 more times!

I only saw Rodney one more time before the Plane of Earth.  On Earth I
used a crystal ball to find the portal and quickly went to Air.

One Air I used confused ?oGD because I didn't want to be immobile for
10 turns while some elemental beat me senseless.  I got engulfed twice
but those E's were no match for +7 Snickersness and a +4 Silver Saber.

On Fire I used a crystal ball and got pummled for ten turns, but I
didn't lose much life over it.

Water worried me because I hadn't genocided ;'s.  I stayed in the air
bubble for a long time hoping the portal was pop over and say hi, but
no such luck.  Eventually I got bored, wielded the Amulet and went
looking for it.  I walked right into Astral without any hot messages.
I wasn't wearing conflict at the time so I kept it off this time and
kept my pet Angel.

On Astral I was attacked by two Arch-Lichs but they didn't do much
before they crumbled into dust.  I replaced my BoS with BoJ and jumped
right, without bothering to check which rider was where.  I figured I
was prepared for all of them and riders are weak anyway (or so I
thought after ascending a wizard recently).

It turns out the right side was guarded by Pestilence and I forgot to
bring any reliable !oEH or !oFH (or B!oH).  Oops!  My WoD took it out
plus some priest and I jumped my way to the temple.  After hacking up
some more priests and angels I got inside and that is when Pestilence
caught up and I almost died from illness.  I mean, I probably did.  I
don't know how many turns it takes, but it was a good three before my
blessed unicorn horn finally worked.

Note to self: Don't quaff *every* !oEH or !oFH for hit points before
going to the planes.

Also, I meleed Pestilence instead of using the WoD.  Why?  Because I'm
stubborn.  I wanted to chop it up!

Pestilence ranks at the top of my list of most dangerous riders now.
He stunned and sicked me, which caused me to zap the WoD all crazy like
all over that high temple.  (See?  I tried it!)  And I normally don't
have !oFH etc. etc. unless something drops it along the way, which is
why I like killing those adventurer monsters.

Famine is in the middle because I normally don't bring a ton of food to
Astral, but I probably bring enough lizard corpses to feed an army.
And I can eat dragons and whatnot.  I'd even go cannibal if I had too.
(I already accidently ate another samurai on the quest).

Death is probably the least scary rider, ironically.  He only drains
permanent hitpoints and I try for at least 300 hp before ascending so I
don't care if he takes a little.  Of course, if I'd gone for Death
first, I would have gone to the wrong altar.  As it turns out, Pesty
was guarding MY altar.

So, fearing for my sammy's life due to a distinct lack of healing
potions, I scrapped plans to clear out Astral and won the game.

Well, first I checked the altar.  I had just read about the player
whose first "ascension" was on the wrong altar because he was drunk on
whiskey at the time.  Then I tried putting the Amulet in the bag of
holding.  It was the REAL ONE, as I'd named it.

Then ....

I checked each again three more times.


Then I offered the Amulet....



